%% TEAM COORDINATION MAP — edit this source; workflow owns the image.
%% Solid arrows are prerequisites; dashed arrows share evidence, not gates.
%% Current hypothesis: native units may support useful explanations; universal cleanliness is not assumed.
flowchart TB
  G["<b>Understand and predict the model's mechanisms</b><br/>Native neurons; attention routes; falsifiable oracle answers.<br/>Legibility ≠ sparsity ≠ causal faithfulness."]
  Q["<b>Freeze a useful behavioral question</b><br/>Qwen3-8B is the main target (MATS); Qwen3-32B the showcase<br/>and validation; 1.7B for development only.<br/>Declare full contexts and answer contrast.<br/>Freeze fitting versus unseen questions/edits and controls.<br/>WHY · test explanations, not universal neuron cleanliness."]
  G --> Q

  subgraph MAIN["PRIMARY PATH · INVESTIGATE, EXPLAIN, TEST"]
    I["<b>Inspect native neurons, attention and downstream readers</b><br/>Original weights, signed poles, full activation contexts.<br/>Trace writers/readers; gate/value regimes where supported.<br/>Attribution proposes candidates; it is not causal proof.<br/>The original model is the measured reference for changes.<br/>OWNER · shared native/tools team / root"]
    F["<b>State a falsifiable explanation</b><br/>Name units, routes, context and predicted intervention effects.<br/>Distinguish observed evidence from an untested hypothesis.<br/>Preserve unexplained cases and competing explanations.<br/>WHY · useful English must commit to checkable predictions."]
    V["<b>Test unseen causal questions and edits</b><br/>Whole-unit or pole ablation, restoration and steering;<br/>attention-route and downstream-reader checks when claimed.<br/>Compare the original model, task controls and near misses.<br/>Report every failure and the collateral effects and total cost."]
    I --> F --> V
  end
  Q --> I

  subgraph LEARN["ORACLE · AMORTIZE VERIFIED INVESTIGATION"]
    O["<b>Read native evidence and answer in English</b><br/>Weight/activation facts and tested mechanisms as inputs.<br/>Compare true, absent and mismatched evidence at matched cost.<br/>Disclosed-answer retrieval is not mechanism proof.<br/>OWNER · native_qa_bridge / oracle team"]
    T["<b>T4 · Train and test oracle transfer (proposed)</b><br/>Checked labels; new contexts/questions/edits; raw answers saved.<br/>Beat AO and AO + interventions at equal passes;<br/>named-neuron claims survive ablation/steering ≥ 80%.<br/>Measure total cost before claiming amortization.<br/>OWNER · shared oracle / AO teams; Path G stays parallel"]
    O --> T
  end
  V --> O
  I -. observations with uncertainty .-> O

  P["<b>MEASURED · neuron input benefit unproven</b><br/>64 edits / 49 contexts; context vectors fixed.<br/>Correct / zero / mismatched: 0.530 / 0.507 / 0.581 nats.<br/>Both primary gain intervals include zero.<br/>7 mismatches nearly identical; all 64 retained.<br/>320 forwards, 38 seconds, free MATS; 1.7B only."]
  R["<b>FIXED · native measurement and labels</b><br/>Full downstream gradients; untested families cannot pass.<br/>Future choices use neuron ablations: no extra forwards.<br/>Signed write readouts are separate from causal effects.<br/>WHY · reliable evidence, explicit scope and honest cost."]
  I -. measurement integrity .-> R
  R -. reliable inputs .-> O
  Q -. current pilot .-> P
  P -. concrete investigation .-> I

  C["<b>Question-scoped neuron circuits · scorecard v2 on Qwen3-8B</b><br/>neuron_scorecard.py: necessity, sufficiency, patching from other<br/>texts, swaps, steering and weight-edit predictions, specificity<br/>on unrelated texts, size; noise-aware floors. Runs on MATS.<br/>MEASURED 1.7B · 11 small hubs: all necessary, none sufficient;<br/>3 are the sink neuron L2.n1821 (10-13 bits on unrelated text).<br/>Not a prerequisite for native explanations. No decomposition.<br/>OWNER · generality"]
  I -. optional product .-> C
  C -. additional validation .-> V

  A["<b>T1 · Atlas decision test (proposed)</b><br/>Random neurons: blind max ≥ 30% of corpus maximum,<br/>near misses below 30%; require ≥ 50% to pass.<br/>1.7B first, then 8B and a 32B sample: cleanliness by size.<br/>Both poles, full windows and sign regimes recorded.<br/>OWNER · shared atlas / explanation team"]
  I -. reuse native evidence .-> A
  A -. tested labels .-> O
  W["<b>T2 · Weak-zeroing test (proposed, not a gate)</b><br/>Per-layer thresholds: mean KL from original ≤ 0.1 bits;<br/>report strong neurons/token, preserve sinks/massive units.<br/>Empirical background variant; atlas can proceed without it.<br/>OWNER · shared native team / root"]
  I -. optional empirical variant .-> W
  S["<b>Qwen3-32B validation and showcase</b><br/>Reproduce Cammarata's published results with our pipeline:<br/>8 negative-pole Santa neurons (removal → 6%) and the<br/>4-neuron preeclampsia hub; then our own circuits there.<br/>Two L40s in bf16 on MATS; RunPod 80 GB only for overflow."]
  I -. same pipeline at 32B .-> S
  S -. validates units and checks .-> V
  K["<b>T3 · Owl edit decision test (proposed)</b><br/>Zero ≤ 50 neurons: unseen-prompt owl mentions 0.95 → ≤ 0.25;<br/>unrelated-prompt KL ≤ 0.05 bits; persona facts intact.<br/>At 8B on fleet's 8B owl organism.<br/>OWNER · existing owl / organism team"]
  V -. flagship application .-> K

  E["<b>IMPLEMENTED · sequence evidence, opt-in</b><br/>Signed neuron activity at every edited position.<br/>One column norm preserves write strength; same forward.<br/>3 neurons / 48 positions: 1,962 prompt tokens in a tiny check.<br/>8B capture job 20658 queued; then matched training.<br/>WHY · test utility on fresh questions, not assume it."]
  E -. informs controls .-> Q
  E -. informs evidence tests .-> O

  L["<b>Measure the entire effort</b><br/>Preprocessing, investigation, interventions and interpretation.<br/>Batch only with draw/metric parity; preserve failures and memory.<br/>OWNER · gpu_launch_review / native_qa_bridge"]
  I -. investigation cost .-> L
  V -. validation cost .-> L
  T -. inference and training cost .-> L
  Z["<b>Success</b><br/>Explanations that survive new causal tests and help answer<br/>useful questions faster; compact circuits are an optional benefit."]
  T --> Z
  L -. cost evidence .-> Z

  classDef goal fill:#173557,stroke:#173557,color:#ffffff,stroke-width:2px;
